To reproduce all nine hashes: run `shasum -a 256 *.zip` in this directory.

Unsupported by design: exact answers of `unzip -t <file>`
----------------------------------------------------------
All four print the same shape; only the "can do" version differs. unzip
refuses on the version-needed field (PK compat.) BEFORE it looks at the method.

  aes128.zip, aes256.zip   (needs v5.1)
    Apple   exit 81
      Archive:  aes128.zip
         skipping: README                  need PK compat. v5.1 (can do v4.5)
      Caution:  zero files tested in aes128.zip.
      1 file skipped because of unsupported compression or encoding.
    Ubuntu  exit 81, identical except "(can do v4.6)"
  lzma.zip                 (needs v6.3, entry vimrc)
    Apple   exit 81, "skipping: vimrc  need PK compat. v6.3 (can do v4.5)", same footer
    Ubuntu  exit 81, same with "(can do v4.6)"
  bzip2.zip                (needs v4.6, entry sample.txt)
    Apple   exit 81, "skipping: sample.txt  need PK compat. v4.6 (can do v4.5)", same footer
    Ubuntu  exit 0: "testing: sample.txt   OK" and
            "No errors detected in compressed data of bzip2.zip."

Coverage gaps
-------------
 * Implode 4K+3 trees and 8K+2 trees: no sample exists in any corpus found;
   hand-built in Task 5 (plan ruling P5).
 * deflate64 match distance > 32 KiB in deflate64-lorem.zip: verified in
   Task 4 (P6).
 * zip2's deflate64_issue_25.zip was rejected: both references reject it
   (exit 3, "missing 2166816915 bytes in zipfile").
